WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.135 --> 00:00:04.670
During a roundtable discussion with the podcast
Skytalkers, Jon Favreau made some interesting

00:00:04.670 --> 00:00:09.340
comments that indicated Grogu and The Mandalorian
had been traveling together for years before

00:00:09.340 --> 00:00:10.800
the finale of Season 2.

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:15.769
It's also implied Grogu spent years in Jedi
training with Luke Skywalker before returning

00:00:15.769 --> 00:00:16.769
to Din Djarin.

00:00:16.769 --> 00:00:17.769
Favreau explained:

00:00:17.769 --> 00:00:21.740
"He started off earlier in the Jedi temple
... and then we know that he's been rescued

00:00:21.740 --> 00:00:23.570
and spent many years with The Mandalorian.

00:00:23.570 --> 00:00:25.020
Went back with Luke.

00:00:25.020 --> 00:00:28.480
Now, we've been two years apart from him there,
training."

00:00:28.480 --> 00:00:32.910
Favreau's comments imply that all of "The
Mandalorian" Season 1 and 2 takes place over

00:00:32.910 --> 00:00:36.379
"many years," which is not directly addressed
in the show.

00:00:36.379 --> 00:00:41.542
It also implies the time jump between Season
2 and "The Book of Boba Fett" is two years long.

00:00:41.542 --> 00:00:46.829
While the exact timeline of "The Mandalorian"
remains unclear, Favreau's use of "many years"

00:00:46.829 --> 00:00:51.789
certainly makes it seem like Grogu and Din
Djarin spent more time together than actually

00:00:51.789 --> 00:00:53.270
seen in "The Mandalorian."

00:00:53.270 --> 00:00:55.560
What kinds of adventures have we missed?

